+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   Channels with very high dynamic range can dominate the derivative calculation if not weighted [S3, unofficial].
+*   The heuristic weight assumption that each channel should have equal influence and contain no outliers may not always be desirable, requiring domain-specific knowledge to adjust weights [S3, unofficial].
+*   Unlike scalar volume rendering, multi-field gradients provide orientation but not absolute direction, and the eigenvector corresponding to the largest eigenvalue can flip direction in local neighborhoods [S3, unofficial]. Therefore, an atmospheric lighting model is used instead of surface-normal-based lighting [S3, unofficial].
 
